  "prompt": "For each percent_off promotion that started in 2025 (promo_type 'percent_off', start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025), give margin_uplift: the gross margin on promotion minus the gross margin in the baseline. A line's gross margin is its net_revenue_eur minus units times unit_cost_eur. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0. Return two columns, in this order: promo_id and margin_uplift. Return one row for each such promotion. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "promo_id",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "margin_uplift",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      }
    ],
    "grain": null
  },
